<title>SINGAPORE: Hup Seng Huat half year falls 47.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Hup Seng Huat half year falls 47.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to Janaury 31, 1997</p>
<p>	   (in  millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		1.79     vs    3.39</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)     0.70     vs    1.40</p>
<p>    Turnover		 35.42     vs   28.95</p>
<p>    Other income	    0.26     vs    0.19</p>
<p>    Interest expense	0.02     vs    0.08</p>
<p>    Operating pretax	2.58     vs    4.72</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.67     vs    1.27</p>
<p>    Minorities		0.13     vs    0.05</p>
<p>Note - Hardware and property investment firm, Hup Seng Huat Co Ltd, said the increased turnover was due to improved export sales while the lower profits were due to lower margins.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
